  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 6,
    "turn_text": "I mean, they have no respect. Three people came up to me and spoke today, and I heard they have no respect for the rule of law. They have no respect for the Constitution, and they certainly don't understand our democracy and what democracy means, because it's a democracy. I mean, when you think about what it really is in the oligards, all of the billionaires, when you think about how this country operates, when you think of us having appropriation in a budget that we are by the Constitution required to do on specific dates to continue this America to operate. We are still negotiating with this, and we only have until March 14th, and the government could shut down. So if we don't negotiate or find at least three people on the other side who will understand in a world that we're living in now, take away fire and police, take away all of the government workers that would no longer be allowed to come to work if we shut down, not alone that they're not going to get a check. And how it's going to affect businesses, and it's going to affect mortgages, it's going to affect car loans, it's going to affect everything that we do. So yes, we have to be prepared for what he's doing.",
