    "turn_idx": 11,
    "turn_text": "I know that Republicans seem to have a great way of communicating with their supporters. have used podcasts and social media and created these networks where people who think alike are communicating with each other. And I know you mentioned this earlier, but have Democrats done enough to really get out there and get their messages across? Like, for instance, the whole idea of the economy. The economy under Biden was strong, but many people going into the election last year didn't feel that way. What can Democrats do? Can they be more forceful in how they communicate? Because certainly Republicans are very, that whole straight talk thing is something that Republicans pride themselves on.",
