  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 12,
    "turn_text": "I think that's an excellent question, and let me just tell you, did we do enough? No. Did we have a message that resonated with the everyday folks? No. Lesson's learned. Part of the reason in the election, people did not believe that Donald Trump would win. Because there was history there, 34 indictments. But then there were people who needed to hear the things he said. Now, there were lies. But if you hear the same thing repeatedly enough, I'm going to make it better. I'm going to cut the fat out of government. All of the things are Our message was to in the weeds. Our message was to symbolic. We had a great tagline. And I said it in just about every speech because I was told to say, we're going to put people over politics. Now, it sounded good in that conference room in Washington, DC. And my grandchild said to me, Grammy, you always say that people were politics. and then the operative words were, what does that mean? And then I said, well, it means we're gonna put food and we're gonna be protecting your mortgage and house. And my grandchild said, why didn't you just say that? That you're not gonna play politics, you're gonna make sure that I can go to school. You're gonna make sure that they keep my lunch program. You're gonna make sure that they keep the funds for communities in school in Ohio. She said, why don't you just say it? And so now, lessons learned. We are now doing podcasts, and I'll give you some good news. I have been selected. We have formed just last Friday a strike team with messaging. Our messaging has to change. You know, we have to do the podcast. We have to be out. We have to do a little bit in a lot of everything. And I've been appointed to the Strike Team Task Force on legislation with another member from Illinois, Sean Caston, who's a brilliant lawyer scholar. And so they paired us up because I'm better at speaking out. I'm better at being creative and coming up with a way to get the message out. So I'm announcing it here. So everyone can hear that, yes, the Democrats, thanks to Jonah Goose and Hakeem Jeffries, have put together a strike team force to come out and to put it in language that relates to everyone. You know, whether you're in the grocery store, whether you're in the barbershop, whether you're in the library, wherever you are, that that message will be strong. But what I can tell you is we're fighting, we're not giving up, and we're not going to stand and let this continue to happen. And we have been able to move the needle somewhat with stopping some of it.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
