  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 16,
    "turn_text": "Well, there's something called the 14th Amendment. There's something called equal opportunity that's written into the Constitution. But here's the thing. It's happening. Some people are afraid in their panicking because people are losing their jobs. They're coming in and saying if diversity, equity and inclusion and accessibility. They're now including people who have disabilities. They're including veterans in this. And they're saying it's also a violation of your freedom of speech because in that Senate bill one, they also say you can't talk about climate. They have buzz words that you can't use in there. So here's what's happening. Just here in our community, we had JP Morgan Chase the other day say they're going to continue with their programs. I was talking to Barbara Benham earlier, and we talked about our local bank, Huntington, and how they're continuing to help people. Comcast just gave me $3 million for a Congressional Black Caucus endowment. of fun. So we have to learn how to change our script. We have to play their game because the end game is to still provide funds and help those and increase our talent pool. So words matter. So if you have diversity, equity, and inclusion, you mentioned Ohio State, President Ted Carter wrote an amazing letter that he will continue to provide equal opportunity. He will continue to broaden the talent base. He will continue to look for folks in various communities and places. And so there will be those who are doing the right thing that will continue to do the right thing. But there will be those who will use this as a state scapegoat because anyone do the right thing anyway. And so we have to stay out there. And it's like playing chess. You know, we are smarter. They just have more money. Donald and Elon Musk have more money, but they are not smarter than us. And at the end, they're gonna get a divorce because Elon Musk is running the show and he's gonna say the wrong thing that Donald Trump won one morning and they're gonna get a divorce. And we're gonna get all the babies and the children. Because we're gonna be right there to divide up their assets and take back what belongs to us. But we have to stay in the game. I know it's scary. People are telling me they're afraid. People are losing their jobs and family members, but we must stay in the game. We know history repeats itself. We have been on this road before. And if you're older, some of us, like I am and others, you have experienced what you thought was the worst thing in your lifetime. And here we are today. We will get through this. And that is the hope that I want you to have. Now, is it going to be easy? I'm not going to lie to you. Absolutely not. Is it going to be scary at times? Yes, but you cannot give up everything that you've done to be in this space, in this place, in what you do.",
