  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 19,
    "turn_text": "Well, let them come. You know, I have a lot of words for many of them. I can't say it here right now. But that's what we have to do back to them. And we also have to tell them, you know, I know some people that said, yeah, I voted for Donald Trump. But I didn't think he was coming after me. You know, and I said, now you're getting just what you deserved. And for those folks who thought it was okay not to vote or to hold their vote, it all goes back to how important your vote in one vote can make a difference. And so we also have to look at those folks who aren't doing the right thing, and we have to say we're not supporting you. You know, if you're not with us and you're not standing up for the American people, I mean, come on, we just celebrated at the end of last year Rosa Parks. If that one little lady could decide that she wasn't going to get on that bus anymore because what they did was wrong. And for 365 days, those folks didn't get on a bus. They needed their money to go to work. They walked. They won the fight. So we have to be willing to win the fight. But you have to be in the fight to win the fight.",
