  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 24,
    "turn_text": "I think you have to call out and you have to write to, don't just send me a letter. You know, send those other folks and they tell us, if I'm in my official capacity, what I can't tell you is to call all those Republicans who are voting the wrong way. Now, I can't tell you that, but because they say don't tell them to just call Republicans. You have to tell them to call all of the Congress people. So, you know, I don't want to violate anything by saying just call the Republicans who aren't voting with you. And I don't mean on your personal, this is not partisan. This is not partisan. This is about someone who is voting to tell you, you can't tell your child what you want them to learn. This is someone who is telling you that they believe it's okay to dismantle the Department of Education. They think it's okay to no longer have Medicare, Medicaid, or Social Security, that it's okay to not put monies into agriculture for the farmers who grow the crop that goes into SNAP programs. It's okay to shut the government down because this administration is protecting the top one and two percent who are billionaires and forget about the rest of us. So you need to call those folks and call them out. You need to write letters to the editorial and put the names in it. When I do something wrong, y'all know how to reach me and say, oh, Congresswoman Beatty, I like you. I didn't like how you voted on this. Or Congresswoman, how come we didn't get the funds from your project and so and so got it. So I want you to do the same thing to everybody. The infrastructure dollars that gave us internet for those children in schools in rural and urban areas that didn't have a laptop. We had people right here in Central Ohio who voted against that. You need to call them out by name, because this is serious, and you need to call them and say, I'm getting ready to write to the local paper, or I'm going to the chamber, the junior league, city hall, to the townships, and I'm calling you out to the voters, because I don't understand why you're not standing up for democracy, why you're not standing up for the rule of law, why you aren't voting to make sure people keep their jobs. And I think that's not part of this, and you have a right to know that, because there are good Democrats and good Republicans who know better. They just need to hear it more from just me.",
