    "turn_idx": 27,
    "turn_text": "to say. Go ahead, Sophia. Thank you so much. Thank you, Karen. Thank you, Congresswoman Beatty. For those in the audience, feel free to join me at the podium if you have questions for Congresswoman. And remember that at CMC, questions have two things in common. One, their 30 seconds are less. And in our great tradition, they end with what type of punctuation? A question mark, absolutely. For those who are joining from Livestream, feel free to text your questions or type them into the chat. I'll get them on my phone. Our first question comes from Ann Hokey. I hope I'm pronouncing her name correctly. What does the House Democratic Party think is the way to cut waste and fraud from executive agencies? And more importantly, what is the Democratic Party's role in raising the debt ceiling in March?",
