    "turn_idx": 30,
    "turn_text": "Well, we're in that process now. We're going to have more litigation. And that's why I said to Karen's question earlier, there's three things Democrats are doing in our messaging. We're communicating, keeping you informed so you know what's real and what's not and what's protected and what's not. And then, unfortunately, there's litigation. when you look at 90 executive orders, and when you look at more than some 50 court cases across this country, and we're winning on many of them, and then there's legislation. We have a bill, I don't know if the title is the best serving, but it's what we have this time to stop the Steel Act. to stop them from stealing everything that they're doing. And it's getting a lot of attention. We have the strike team because we still have a government that's working in our legal system. We still have attorney generals who are banning together from multiple states and they're making progress. Thank you for that question.",
