  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, one of the things that we're doing, I feel I assume from what you said the same way that you are, but here's the question. The Congress is the Republican Party right now. They are the only ones that can bring a bill to the floor. They're the only ones that can approve a bill to go into a committee. And so one of the things we have to do is start asking that question to all of the Congress. So often, we're the ones holding the town halls because we're not afraid to come out and tell you, here's what we're doing and when we're wrong, we're wrong. You know, we've all made mistakes, but that question, whether it's Ukraine, whether it's what JD Vance, who came from Ohio, is doing right now in Europe. What he's doing, we're trying to take away the freedom of speech and stirring up all this. And I think they're doing this, whether it's the Ukraine, whether it's Gaza, whether it's anything else that we're looking at that just treads on us because it's so wrong. They're doing that to sidetrack us and get the attention while they're coming back and undergirding everything else. Education, health care, think about the things they're going after, treasury. CFPB, education. I mean, just think about if you wipe out Social Security and Medicare. You're just talking about poor people. Look at what they're saying about immigration. They're doing everything to dismantle and get rid of everything that they can have control. And let me tell you why it's not going to work. When they're firing all these people that are the threading the needle to how this country runs, and they're getting rid of them, who's going to then run the country? It won't work for them because they don't have unless we allow them to your question. If we don't write that Ukraine or that European question to every member of Congress and tell them to stop, so you have to be stronger language, to stop because you have a vote. And we have an off-year presidential election coming back. In 2026, we're in the fight for our life now. So if you don't get out there and make sure that you vote and vote for people who are going to stand up, not just for us. This is about the American people. My role is to protect the people. And so you have to vote because we could take back the House. And if we took back the House and the Senate, then I can give you a better answer because we would be in charge and I could give you the hope. And I could tell you, as we've done before, Donald Trump put those executive orders in when he was the president before. Joe Biden came in and undid everyone of those executive orders. Our unemployment rate was lower than it had ever been. Our inflation, our economy, according to Jay Powell, chair of the Federal Reserve, we were in a good place. And look at us now.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
