  {
    "episode_id": 77013,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 38,
    "turn_text": "It's interesting because we are as diverse as this room. Calls always work for me because somebody picks up the phone in our offices and don't be offended if you get a staff person or a chief of staff when you go in stronger with them because every member is not going to see you or they're not going to answer the phone. So you have to say, I'm a voter. And if you talk into those folks, I can't tell you just to call the Republicans. But if you're talking to those other folks, you tell them, and the same thing you tell Democrats, because all Democrats might not be on the right page. So you tell them, I'm a voter. I'm writing down your boss's name, and we are not going to stand for this. And if he loses, you lose a job. And then you tell him, and I'm going to call back tomorrow to ask you for the answer that you said to your boss. Just keep calling. It frustrates the heck out of staff, senior staff. And then you know what they do? They call and say, Congresswoman, can you call Mrs. Clark back? Because she don't call here every day. And they're human. And the junior staff that answers the phone, they get scared and emotional. They say, oh, no, somebody used a bad word at me. And somebody screamed at me. And then they come in, you know, they're 25, 26 years old. And they'll say, Congresswoman, are we really taking people's health care? So I say, yeah, they're going to take yours. So let's get with the program. And then we call the people back. Now, if you have emails, that still works. But I tell you what works because we have to live by social media now. Whether you like it or not, social media, fortunately and unfortunately, still is a way that a lot of people get their information. But then there are those of us who do legacy media. I listen to the radio. I watch CNN. I watch C-SPAN. I watch MSNBC. I watch Fox on some days. Because I need to know what America's thinking. Not just Democrats, but Democrats, Republicans, independents, the far progressives. So I think you have to divide it up. But you don't stop. You have to be consistent and you have to do it often. You have to make us as angry as you should be. And that's what works.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_03",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
