    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/7/77013.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 46,
    "turn_text": "That is not off the table. But right now, that is not off the table. And you know, I'm not just saying this, we have had I'm gonna mess up the number five impeachment managers in the last five or six years to do this. But it is a lot different as a sitting president. Come on, let me just be real here. You had a person who was a former president with 34 indictments. I don't know about you, but if any brother in this room had an indictment of one or two, he'd be incarcerated, okay? So. We don't want to be performative and theatrical only, but we do know it grits at Donald Trump. We do know that he can't take the same game he puts out there. And so one of the things that we're trying to do is litigate and legislate as much as we can, but it is not off the table because people like your mother and parents with children, we can't take anything off the table to save their lives. And so whether it is looking at impeachment, whether it is the strike team, whether it is the media team, we are saying to them, we are not afraid, and I've used those words, we're coming after you. And they don't like it. Now, nobody from the administration should be called a little Joyce Beatty back. But they have several of us as members on their list. That's a good sign. Now, my staff over here thinks it's a bad sign because I have to have so much security around me in big public places and they come to my home and all of that kind of stuff. But it works, whether it is the impeachment, whether it is the lawsuits with the attorney generals, whether it's us protesting, because it doesn't matter how insensitive, unintelligent, or crazy you are, nobody likes the personal attacks. And Donald Trump has a problem when people say he's not in charge. And so right now, we're going after Elon Musk to make sure that upsets Donald Trump.",
