    "turn_text": "Here's the thing, there are two new senators and it is easy to get through to them the same way. Their offices are listed and you call them and you say, hey look, John Hughstead, you're not even in your own term. You know, you fulfill it. They're fulfilling terms. So they have to run in their own right. And so you need to be really strong with them. Well, you got these little appointments. You have to come before the people. And we, and you have to tell them what you expect them to do. John Houston, you have children. How could you do this? And I think those are the kinds of things you have to commit them strong. You email them, you call them, you protest them. They have offices in the state of Ohio. They have staff that works out of Columbus. You know, you send them letters with big markers, big red, that we are not. You do things to get their attention. They're scaring you. When I came in here, at least six people came up to me and said, Congresswoman, I'm scared or I'm a little scared or should I be scared. You want to scare them and you tell them the power of your vote.",
